  "goodToKnow": "Der Krapfen is a fried, jam-filled doughnut, called Krapfen in Bavaria and Austria, Berliner in much of Germany, and Pfannkuchen in Berlin itself (where Pfannkuchen elsewhere means pancake). They're eaten especially at Fasching; a prank is to fill one with mustard. The plural is the same."
